      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>FGL 27M S &amp; 1M E OF FENCE POST

ASC CAP FLUSH W/GRND 27M S &amp; 1M E OF FENCE POST ALONG SOUTH BANK OF KENNEDALE RAVINE.

 elevation 644.8m</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684648904">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP385 Kennedale Ravine&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finding this brass cap was a gong show right from the time we left BCP768 to within metres of the cap itself.  The list is too long to go into and we can only hope there were no witnesses to parts of it!  The drive over was full of interesting sights while the GPS lost its stubborn little mind over our route.  Later we found it was set for the wrong cap, but fortunately Mr Shark knew where he wanted to go and how he wanted to get there.  How we dealt with the construction blockages near GZ was hilarious (or alarming) to any onlookers, but no one got hurt and hopefully no one witnessed the whole circus act.  The last leg to GZ went very smoothly and another tough search was averted thanks to quickly spotting the stake and finding the cap right at its base.  Thanks for the laughs, sights along the way and the cap, outforthehunt.  We were fortunate to come away unscathed and able to carry on!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684211280">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP385 Kennedale Ravine

Out again this evening to get a few more BCPs. We drove through a torrential downpour on the way here. We lucked out that the rain let up as we approached the cap. We found a place to park then hurried to avoid another downpour. We followed the red chip trail to a fence blocking the way. Found the gap in the fence and then the cap. It's in great shape and nicely has a stake next to it. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for all the BCPs and the fun I've had over the last couple weeks getting most of the ones in the Edmonton area. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
